   {
    "name": "Path steps",
    "html": "<h2>Path: Zero to Kernel in C</h2><p>C basics to a real kernel in C.</p><p>Follow the steps in order — each builds on the last.</p><ol><li><a href=\"https://osdev.sektor9.dev/synthesized_tutorials/00-introduction/01-how-a-computer-boots/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">1. How a computer boots</a> <em>(🟢)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://osdev.sektor9.dev/synthesized_tutorials/00-introduction/02-your-toolchain/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2. Your toolchain</a> <em>(🟢)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLowKtXNTBypGqImE405J2565dvjafglHU\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">3. Ben Eater's 8-bit computer</a> <em>(🟢)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://www.knking.com/books/c2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">4. C pointers &amp; memory</a> <em>(🟢)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://www.tutorialspoint.com/assembly_programming/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">5. Reading assembly (NASM)</a> <em>(🟠)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://pages.cs.wisc.edu/~remzi/OSTEP/intro.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">6. What is an operating system?</a> <em>(🟢)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/Bare_Bones\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">7. OSDev Wiki Bare Bones</a> <em>(🟠)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://tuhdo.github.io/os01/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">8. Operating Systems: From 0 to 1 (os01)</a> <em>(🟠)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://littleosbook.github.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">9. The Little OS Book</a> <em>(🟠)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://osdev.sektor9.dev/synthesized_tutorials/concepts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10. VGA text mode</a> <em>(🟠)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/Global_Descriptor_Table\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">11. GDT &amp; protected mode</a> <em>(🟠)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/Printing_To_Screen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">12. Build a simple print + panic</a> <em>(🟠)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://pages.cs.wisc.edu/~remzi/OSTEP/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">13. Memory management</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/Setting_Up_Paging\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">14. Paging in your kernel</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://osdev.sektor9.dev/synthesized_tutorials/concepts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">15. Interrupts &amp; the IDT</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://github.com/Exclavia/Kernel-Dev\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">16. James Molloy's Kernel Tutorials</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://osdev.sektor9.dev/synthesized_tutorials/concepts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">17. Build a scheduler</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/User_Mode\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">18. User mode &amp; syscalls</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li></ol><p><em>Mirror of the interactive docs learning path · sektor9.dev</em></p>"
   }
