   {
    "name": "Path steps",
    "html": "<h2>Path: Embedded C &amp; Rust</h2><p>Professional embedded C then Rust.</p><p>Follow the steps in order — each builds on the last.</p><ol><li><a href=\"https://users.ece.utexas.edu/~valvano/Volume1/E-Book/Cover_edn8.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">1. Embedded Systems: Shape the World</a> <em>(🟠)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://github.com/MYaqoobEmbedded/STM32-Tutorials\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2. STM32 register programming</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://ptolemy.berkeley.edu/books/leeseshia/releases/LeeSeshia_DigitalV2_2.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">3. Introduction to Embedded Systems (Lee &amp; Seshia)</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/handle/20.500.12657/46817/2021_Book_EmbeddedSystemDesign.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">4. Embedded System Design (Springer, open access)</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://github.com/MYaqoobEmbedded/STM32-Tutorials\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">5. The linker script</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://docs.rust-embedded.org/book/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">6. The Embedded Rust Book</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://docs.esp-rs.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">7. Rust on ESP32</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://docs.rs/embedded-hal/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">8. svd2rust &amp; HALs</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://elecdocs.sektor9.dev/synthesized/embedded-rust/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">9. Embedded Rust in action</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://embassy.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10. Embassy (async embedded)</a> <em>(⚫)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://openocd.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">11. Debugging with JTAG</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://www.freertos.org/Documentation/RTOS_book.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">12. RTOS integration</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://www.allaboutcircuits.com/textbook/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">13. Reading schematics &amp; datasheets</a> <em>(🔴)</em></li><li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">14. CI for firmware</a> <em>(🟠)</em></li></ol><p><em>Mirror of the interactive docs learning path · sektor9.dev</em></p>"
